### 2. Poor naming — all 10 tests (lines 17–88)

Every test is named `Xxx_Works`. This says nothing about the scenario or expected outcome. When a test fails, you learn "`UpdatePrice_Works` failed" — but not *what* about updating a price was being verified.

| Current | Suggested |
|---------|-----------|
| `AddProduct_Works` | `AddProduct_NewSku_IsRetrievable` |
| `GetProduct_Works` | `GetProduct_ExistingSku_ReturnsCorrectProduct` |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | `UpdatePrice_ExistingSku_PriceIsUpdated` |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | `RemoveProduct_ExistingSku_NoLongerRetrievable` |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | `GetProductCount_AfterAdding_ReturnsCorrectCount` |
